1
00:00:00,484 --> 00:00:01,484
(All characters and organisations in this drama are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,484 --> 00:00:02,484
(Filming with minors followed broadcast guidelines,)

3
00:00:02,484 --> 00:00:03,584
(and generative AI was used in select scenes.)

4
00:00:04,844 --> 00:00:06,184
I hope we don't see each other...

5
00:00:06,244 --> 00:00:07,784
(Episode 6)

6
00:00:07,944 --> 00:00:09,084
like this again.

7
00:00:12,014 --> 00:00:13,514
I have a question.

8
00:00:16,784 --> 00:00:17,784
Is it possible...

9
00:00:19,314 --> 00:00:20,314
he's my son?

10
00:00:23,544 --> 00:00:24,614
Is Gyeol...

11
00:00:25,384 --> 00:00:26,484
my son?

12
00:00:30,984 --> 00:00:33,184
No. My Gyeol is my son.

13
00:00:33,814 --> 00:00:36,184
He has nothing to do with you, Kim Mu Jin.

14
00:00:42,084 --> 00:00:43,114
Gyeol said...

15
00:00:43,614 --> 00:00:44,944
he's eight years old.

16
00:00:45,844 --> 00:00:47,144
We broke up eight years ago.

17
00:00:52,414 --> 00:00:55,084
Were you cheating on me when we were together?

18
00:00:57,814 --> 00:01:00,244
I started dating Heung Sik right after we broke up.

19
00:01:00,784 --> 00:01:01,784
That's a lie.

20
00:01:03,444 --> 00:01:05,284
The Han Gyu Rim I know...

21
00:01:06,644 --> 00:01:08,714
isn't evil enough to cheat,

22
00:01:09,684 --> 00:01:11,554
nor is she shameless enough to start dating someone else...

23
00:01:11,614 --> 00:01:13,284
right after we broke up.

24
00:01:16,814 --> 00:01:18,414
You think you know me so well?

25
00:01:19,284 --> 00:01:20,844
If you know me so well,

26
00:01:21,144 --> 00:01:22,644
how did you end up getting betrayed?

27
00:01:24,544 --> 00:01:26,484
After everything that happened eight years ago,

28
00:01:26,714 --> 00:01:28,514
you still haven't learned your lesson?

29
00:01:30,944 --> 00:01:32,344
You're still living this pathetic life...

30
00:01:32,884 --> 00:01:34,644
because you're so foolish.

31
00:01:35,614 --> 00:01:37,544
I thought you were smart, but you're completely clueless.

32
00:01:38,214 --> 00:01:40,014
You should be getting angry and cursing me out.

33
00:01:40,584 --> 00:01:42,384
Tell me that your life was ruined by meeting me...

34
00:01:43,044 --> 00:01:44,584
and that you'll kill me if you ever see me again.

35
00:01:44,644 --> 00:01:45,984
Get angry and yell at me.

36
00:01:46,984 --> 00:01:49,984
Stop wasting your time going after someone else's son.

37
00:01:51,314 --> 00:01:53,044
Can I get a paternity test for Gyeol?

38
00:01:54,284 --> 00:01:55,584
Are you not listening to me?

39
00:01:55,684 --> 00:01:56,844
A paternity test.

40
00:01:59,114 --> 00:02:00,284
I'm asking if I can get one.

41
00:02:06,014 --> 00:02:08,014
(List Of Wedding Gifts And Furnishings)

42
00:02:14,014 --> 00:02:16,314
Don't you think this is a bit much?

43
00:02:17,214 --> 00:02:18,954
What's so much about it?

44
00:02:19,384 --> 00:02:21,044
For my mom, this is actually pretty modest.

45
00:02:22,344 --> 00:02:26,614
Getting high-end designer crocodile bags for all the aunts...

46
00:02:27,044 --> 00:02:28,514
doesn't seem very modest, does it?

47
00:02:29,884 --> 00:02:30,914
Do you want to change it?

48
00:02:31,454 --> 00:02:33,584
Then how about you buy the apartment, Gyu Young?

49
00:02:34,414 --> 00:02:35,414
No.

50
00:02:36,314 --> 00:02:41,884
I just didn't realise there would be 25 aunts.

51
00:02:52,144 --> 00:02:54,244
Your family must be really close.

52
00:02:54,744 --> 00:02:55,944
Yes, pretty much.

53
00:03:11,214 --> 00:03:12,214
Mom.

54
00:03:17,144 --> 00:03:18,144
Ms. Han Gyu Rim.

55
00:03:18,544 --> 00:03:19,544
Gyeol.

56
00:03:21,314 --> 00:03:22,584
Are you making hamburgers?

57
00:03:24,384 --> 00:03:25,384
Yes.

58
00:03:27,444 --> 00:03:29,814
What did you talk about with that man?

59
00:03:32,114 --> 00:03:33,744
He just said he was sorry...

60
00:03:33,814 --> 00:03:35,314
for calling you over without telling me.

61
00:03:35,414 --> 00:03:38,384
See? He apologised. I told you so.

62
00:03:38,814 --> 00:03:41,014
I told you he's a really nice guy.

63
00:03:42,884 --> 00:03:44,484
Don't you ever see that man again.

64
00:03:44,844 --> 00:03:45,844
Why?

65
00:03:46,144 --> 00:03:48,144
Just don't see him because I said so.

66
00:03:48,584 --> 00:03:49,784
But why?

67
00:03:51,614 --> 00:03:54,684
Han Gyeol, why won't you listen to me today?

68
00:03:54,844 --> 00:03:56,184
I don't like that man.

69
00:03:56,544 --> 00:03:59,014
So I don't like you meeting him either.

70
00:04:00,114 --> 00:04:02,184
Why do you hate him so much?

71
00:04:04,084 --> 00:04:06,314
I don't know. I just do.

72
00:04:06,644 --> 00:04:09,714
- Okay? - No. I don't get it at all.

73
00:04:13,614 --> 00:04:14,714
Promise me...

74
00:04:14,984 --> 00:04:16,644
that you won't see that man again.

75
00:04:19,614 --> 00:04:22,644
Han Gyeol, are you really not going to promise me?

76
00:04:23,584 --> 00:04:27,984
Give me a reason I can accept, then I won't see him anymore.

77
00:04:30,284 --> 00:04:31,584
And to be honest,

78
00:04:31,584 --> 00:04:36,314
store-bought hamburgers are way tastier than yours.

79
00:04:39,944 --> 00:04:41,784
Who does he get that stubbornness from?

80
00:04:42,144 --> 00:04:43,544
The nerve of that little squirt.

81
00:04:54,944 --> 00:04:56,384
Who's there?

82
00:04:59,514 --> 00:05:01,714
What are you doing sitting in the dark?

83
00:05:01,784 --> 00:05:02,814
I thought you were a ghost.

84
00:05:05,414 --> 00:05:08,184
When you left earlier, you were like a guy going on his first date,

85
00:05:08,254 --> 00:05:09,714
all thrilled with the world.

86
00:05:11,044 --> 00:05:12,784
What did you say to the kid?

87
00:05:13,984 --> 00:05:16,084
Did you say, "I am your father"?

88
00:05:20,684 --> 00:05:23,484
Right. No matter how much you're losing it,

89
00:05:23,544 --> 00:05:25,684
you wouldn't ask a kid something like that.

90
00:05:26,744 --> 00:05:28,114
I asked Gyu Rim.

91
00:05:31,114 --> 00:05:32,184
She said he's not my son.

92
00:05:33,014 --> 00:05:35,544
So then what? Is he that monkey-faced guy's son?

93
00:05:35,814 --> 00:05:36,984
Was she cheating on you?

94
00:05:37,614 --> 00:05:39,584
Gyu Rim says no.

95
00:05:41,444 --> 00:05:43,244
But I don't believe her.

96
00:05:43,844 --> 00:05:46,184
Right. I think she's lying too.

97
00:05:48,184 --> 00:05:52,014
No. I can't lose my head over this too.

98
00:05:52,844 --> 00:05:53,844
It's just...

99
00:05:54,884 --> 00:05:56,444
We even have the same taste in hamburgers.

100
00:05:56,984 --> 00:05:58,784
No pickled onions, add a fried egg.

101
00:05:58,844 --> 00:06:01,014
No pickled onions, add a fried egg.

102
00:06:01,814 --> 00:06:04,244
That's how I like them too. Does that make me your son?

103
00:06:06,044 --> 00:06:07,044
You're right.

104
00:06:07,444 --> 00:06:10,814
What is wrong with me?

105
00:06:11,844 --> 00:06:13,544
When someone says no, I should just accept it,

106
00:06:13,614 --> 00:06:15,044
and know when to give up.

107
00:06:17,984 --> 00:06:20,714
Why am I still hung up on a married woman?

108
00:06:23,184 --> 00:06:24,444
Am I crazy or what?

109
00:06:25,214 --> 00:06:27,084
Of course you are. You're definitely crazy.

110
00:06:27,314 --> 00:06:29,214
Seo Hyun, Yoon Jin,

111
00:06:29,284 --> 00:06:31,314
and none of them think you're sane right now.

112
00:06:31,544 --> 00:06:34,744
If you get any crazier, I'll have you committed myself.

113
00:06:53,814 --> 00:06:55,884
Get up. Hurry up and get up.

114
00:06:56,214 --> 00:06:57,984
What do you think you're doing sleeping here?

115
00:06:58,884 --> 00:07:00,614
What's all that noise?

116
00:07:00,684 --> 00:07:03,314
I went to bed in the early morning. Don't wake me up. It's Sunday.

117
00:07:03,484 --> 00:07:07,414
You can sleep at your own house. Please get out of my house now.

118
00:07:08,214 --> 00:07:11,484
What is this nonsense so early in the morning?

119
00:07:11,484 --> 00:07:15,314
- I'm asking you to get out now. - Han Gyu Rim.

120
00:07:15,644 --> 00:07:16,644
Do I know you?

121
00:07:16,844 --> 00:07:18,714
What's this new act?

122
00:07:21,844 --> 00:07:23,214
What?

123
00:07:23,314 --> 00:07:27,284
I've already packed your things, so just get up and leave.

124
00:07:27,584 --> 00:07:30,184
- The exit is this way. - Are you crazy?

125
00:07:30,214 --> 00:07:31,584
You're the crazy one,

126
00:07:31,644 --> 00:07:34,314
sleeping in late in someone else's house.

127
00:07:34,744 --> 00:07:38,044
- Want to get lost, or get beat up? - Darn...

128
00:07:41,744 --> 00:07:43,184
Are you doing this because of the family meeting yesterday?

129
00:07:43,284 --> 00:07:44,744
Because I didn't let Dad and you come?

130
00:07:44,814 --> 00:07:46,244
Are you being this childish because you're sulking?

131
00:07:46,314 --> 00:07:47,944
Who do you think you are to call him Dad?

132
00:07:48,584 --> 00:07:50,184
You have your own dad.

133
00:07:50,184 --> 00:07:51,344
"Dad."

134
00:07:51,514 --> 00:07:53,584
You were practically oozing with affection.

135
00:07:53,784 --> 00:07:55,384
What are you talking about?

136
00:07:58,214 --> 00:07:59,214
You saw it?

137
00:07:59,314 --> 00:08:02,584
Get out. Now. I've never had a sister like you,

138
00:08:02,784 --> 00:08:05,614
and Father has never had a daughter like you. Get out.

139
00:08:05,614 --> 00:08:08,744
You were at the family meeting? What exactly did you see?

140
00:08:10,384 --> 00:08:12,684
No matter how much you're ashamed of us,

141
00:08:12,814 --> 00:08:15,544
how could you hire an actor for your wedding events?

142
00:08:15,644 --> 00:08:18,914
Did you go through all that trouble in medical school,

143
00:08:18,984 --> 00:08:21,584
- study abroad to be a con artist? - Darn it.

144
00:08:21,844 --> 00:08:24,114
Before I go and tell your boyfriend's family everything,

145
00:08:24,114 --> 00:08:26,044
you'd better tell them the truth and ask for forgiveness.

146
00:08:26,144 --> 00:08:28,014
If you're that ashamed of our family,

147
00:08:28,414 --> 00:08:31,584
then for the rest of our lives, we'll stay out of your life.

148
00:08:31,744 --> 00:08:33,544
So you might as well say you've cut ties with us.

149
00:08:57,984 --> 00:08:59,514
What do you mean by that?

150
00:09:01,684 --> 00:09:04,944
I went to the family meeting even though you told me not to go.

151
00:09:07,614 --> 00:09:08,814
You did the right thing.

152
00:09:10,044 --> 00:09:11,044
Wait.

153
00:09:11,644 --> 00:09:12,944
That's it?

154
00:09:15,914 --> 00:09:20,684
I can only imagine how much you agonized before you went.

155
00:09:21,114 --> 00:09:22,814
I knew you didn't want to go,

156
00:09:22,884 --> 00:09:25,114
but you must have felt you had no choice...

157
00:09:25,884 --> 00:09:27,184
and that must have been hard for you.

158
00:09:29,484 --> 00:09:30,714
Do you need me to say more?

159
00:09:32,184 --> 00:09:33,184
Well...

160
00:09:34,614 --> 00:09:36,214
It was Gyu Young's family meeting.

161
00:09:36,814 --> 00:09:38,284
The girl's name was Gyu Young...

162
00:09:42,914 --> 00:09:43,914
Who did you say?

163
00:09:44,854 --> 00:09:45,854
That's right.

164
00:09:46,784 --> 00:09:48,114
It's not someone else with the same name.

165
00:09:48,214 --> 00:09:50,144
And you weren't confused or mistaken.

166
00:09:50,814 --> 00:09:53,414
It's the one you thought of as soon as you heard the name.

167
00:09:54,614 --> 00:09:56,014
Your daughter, Han Gyu Young.

168
00:09:58,914 --> 00:10:00,284
You went to her family meeting?

169
00:10:01,814 --> 00:10:02,884
Why would you do that?

170
00:10:04,614 --> 00:10:06,114
What about her father?

171
00:10:11,414 --> 00:10:14,214
Where was her father that you had to go instead?

172
00:10:14,484 --> 00:10:15,714
Well, I'm not sure,

173
00:10:15,784 --> 00:10:17,944
but it seemed like there were some circumstances.

174
00:10:20,084 --> 00:10:21,914
Did Gyu Young ask you to?

175
00:10:28,944 --> 00:10:30,854
What on earth was she thinking...

176
00:10:33,384 --> 00:10:35,854
How did you and Gyu Young meet?

177
00:10:37,784 --> 00:10:38,944
To be honest,

178
00:10:40,744 --> 00:10:41,854
she came to see me...

179
00:10:41,854 --> 00:10:43,484
after she found out that we got married...

180
00:10:44,484 --> 00:10:45,714
nine years ago.

181
00:10:47,984 --> 00:10:49,044
Oh my goodness.

182
00:10:49,984 --> 00:10:52,384
Why didn't you tell me back then?

183
00:10:52,444 --> 00:10:55,914
Because Gyu Young asked me never to tell you.

184
00:10:58,144 --> 00:11:01,044
And then, she called me recently for the first time in a long while.

185
00:11:01,684 --> 00:11:03,714
I never meant to deceive you.

186
00:11:04,814 --> 00:11:06,514
I was just waiting for the right time...

187
00:11:06,584 --> 00:11:07,644
to tell you everything.

188
00:11:08,744 --> 00:11:11,844
Anyway, after going to the family meeting,

189
00:11:12,114 --> 00:11:13,914
I knew I couldn't put this off any longer,

190
00:11:13,914 --> 00:11:15,314
so I'm telling you now.

191
00:11:16,244 --> 00:11:17,244
Honey,

192
00:11:18,144 --> 00:11:20,214
I'm sorry I didn't tell you sooner.

193
00:11:27,144 --> 00:11:28,144
Honey.

194
00:11:29,784 --> 00:11:30,784
Honey.

195
00:11:35,984 --> 00:11:39,044
Why are you the one apologising?

196
00:11:39,744 --> 00:11:41,444
I'm the one who should be sorry.

197
00:11:42,244 --> 00:11:44,014
You're just making me feel worse.

198
00:11:52,114 --> 00:11:53,984
For putting you in such a difficult position,

199
00:11:54,844 --> 00:11:56,444
I'm so sorry.

200
00:11:57,614 --> 00:12:01,984
No, why would you say that? Honey,

201
00:12:02,644 --> 00:12:04,844
your children are my children.

202
00:12:04,914 --> 00:12:07,144
That's why I went to the family meeting.

203
00:12:07,744 --> 00:12:09,844
I'm a father too, you know?

204
00:12:10,284 --> 00:12:11,844
It's okay. Don't say that.

205
00:12:13,044 --> 00:12:15,884
The family meeting went well, so it's all right.

206
00:12:29,784 --> 00:12:30,784
Han Gyu Rim.

207
00:12:31,044 --> 00:12:32,714
Just you dare breathe a word to my boyfriend's family.

208
00:12:33,044 --> 00:12:35,284
If you do, we're both dead.

209
00:12:41,784 --> 00:12:43,644
What other choice did I have? What choice?

210
00:12:43,784 --> 00:12:44,784
Calling yourselves my family,

211
00:12:44,844 --> 00:12:46,084
all you've ever done is cause me trouble.

212
00:12:46,144 --> 00:12:48,084
What on earth have any of you ever done for me?

213
00:12:48,144 --> 00:12:49,314
When I've been struggling,

214
00:12:49,384 --> 00:12:50,984
have anyone in this family ever given me a single dime?

215
00:13:02,844 --> 00:13:04,814
(List Of Wedding Gifts And Furnishings)

216
00:13:06,644 --> 00:13:08,684
What am I going to do about the gifts?

217
00:13:11,444 --> 00:13:12,484
Darn it.

218
00:13:12,844 --> 00:13:13,914
Han Gyu Oh.

219
00:13:16,444 --> 00:13:17,684
Where did he go?

220
00:13:45,084 --> 00:13:47,414
This is nicer than most boutiques.

221
00:14:06,914 --> 00:14:08,044
What are you doing?

222
00:14:09,544 --> 00:14:11,884
What do you mean?

223
00:14:12,214 --> 00:14:14,484
I was just looking. You have a lot of nice things.

224
00:14:14,584 --> 00:14:15,814
Lately, oversized fits...

225
00:14:15,884 --> 00:14:18,114
and the boyfriend look have seemed so nice.

226
00:14:19,614 --> 00:14:21,584
You're the one who always wears clothes so tight...

227
00:14:21,644 --> 00:14:23,314
it looks like you're cutting off your circulation.

228
00:14:23,884 --> 00:14:24,984
All of a sudden?

229
00:14:25,614 --> 00:14:27,314
I mean, if you wanted to try the boyfriend look,

230
00:14:27,384 --> 00:14:29,584
wear your boyfriend's clothes. Why go through my closet?

231
00:14:29,744 --> 00:14:32,784
I'm not going through it. I told you, I was just looking.

232
00:14:34,084 --> 00:14:36,484
I guess you do your looking with your hands, not your eyes.

233
00:14:39,014 --> 00:14:40,014
For someone who was just looking,

234
00:14:40,084 --> 00:14:42,584
it's amazing how you only picked out the expensive stuff.

235
00:14:43,944 --> 00:14:46,584
And I doubt these would fit your boyfriend.

236
00:14:49,444 --> 00:14:50,444
Why?

237
00:14:50,644 --> 00:14:52,144
Were you planning to sell them behind my back?

238
00:14:54,514 --> 00:14:56,984
Darn it. You’re being so petty, and I don't need these anymore.

239
00:14:57,244 --> 00:14:59,284
Why? You need money?

240
00:15:00,314 --> 00:15:02,514
How much do you need that you'd go through my closet?

241
00:15:05,014 --> 00:15:06,014
Do you have any money?

242
00:15:06,114 --> 00:15:07,214
By any chance, how much could you lend...

243
00:15:07,314 --> 00:15:10,044
No, I mean, can't you just lend me everything you have?

244
00:15:10,214 --> 00:15:12,214
You know my future husband's family is completely loaded.

245
00:15:12,944 --> 00:15:14,814
1 year? No, 6 months?

246
00:15:15,014 --> 00:15:16,914
No, I can pay you back everything within three months.

247
00:15:17,084 --> 00:15:19,184
Gyu Oh, you're doing well for yourself.

248
00:15:19,414 --> 00:15:21,444
If you say you're having a hard time or need something,

249
00:15:21,544 --> 00:15:23,414
there are plenty of women who'd give you anything.

250
00:15:23,484 --> 00:15:26,084
You can easily make thousands if you want to.

251
00:15:27,414 --> 00:15:30,214
I'm not asking for a handout, I'm asking for a loan.

252
00:15:30,614 --> 00:15:32,014
I'll pay you double the bank's interest.

253
00:15:34,444 --> 00:15:35,684
You know...

254
00:15:36,684 --> 00:15:38,044
exactly how I earn this money,

255
00:15:38,844 --> 00:15:41,314
and you're okay with that?

256
00:15:41,944 --> 00:15:43,184
Could you use that money guilt-free?

257
00:15:44,214 --> 00:15:45,244
What?

258
00:15:46,314 --> 00:15:48,414
Someone else called it dirty money,

259
00:15:48,814 --> 00:15:50,984
and said he couldn't accept it.

260
00:15:52,014 --> 00:15:53,284
What are you talking about?

261
00:15:54,514 --> 00:15:56,884
It just feels like that he is my real family.

262
00:15:59,784 --> 00:16:01,384
So what am I, fake family?

263
00:16:02,044 --> 00:16:04,684
I'm just being cool and accepting what you do,

264
00:16:04,684 --> 00:16:05,884
and acknowledging it.

265
00:16:05,944 --> 00:16:07,714
- Get out. - Gyu Oh.

266
00:16:07,784 --> 00:16:11,244
- I don't want to talk. Get out. - Han Gyu Oh.

267
00:16:11,244 --> 00:16:12,614
Even if I were rolling in money,

268
00:16:13,814 --> 00:16:15,984
I wouldn't give you a single dime, so get out now.

269
00:16:16,044 --> 00:16:17,444
- Hey. - Now.

270
00:16:27,144 --> 00:16:28,684
Did anyone force you to earn money that way?

271
00:16:29,144 --> 00:16:30,344
You're the one who chose to live like that.

272
00:16:31,684 --> 00:16:35,384
If you didn't want to lend it, you should've just said so.

273
00:16:35,684 --> 00:16:37,244
You're making me out to be some kind of monster.

274
00:16:40,884 --> 00:16:41,884
Darn it.

275
00:16:42,114 --> 00:16:43,114
I don't know now...

276
00:16:58,414 --> 00:17:03,144
- Get a grip, Han Gyu Rim. Okay? - I have a bad feeling about this.

277
00:17:03,714 --> 00:17:08,384
Hey, you stay here. I'll go there instead.

278
00:17:08,814 --> 00:17:11,214
No, it's okay. Everything is ready.

279
00:17:11,344 --> 00:17:12,344
Will you be okay?

280
00:17:14,884 --> 00:17:16,214
I'm off to make a delivery.

281
00:17:16,414 --> 00:17:18,884
Hey, when things are tough, it's hard to even smile.

282
00:17:19,054 --> 00:17:20,784
Don't force yourself to smile.

283
00:17:21,484 --> 00:17:24,744
Oh dear. Is she going through a hard time again?

284
00:17:25,914 --> 00:17:28,784
Who made her upset now?

285
00:17:31,314 --> 00:17:32,384
Grandma.

286
00:17:33,814 --> 00:17:35,444
Oh, your mom just stepped out.

287
00:17:36,554 --> 00:17:40,014
Hey, why are you holding your back like that?

288
00:17:40,184 --> 00:17:42,314
I tweaked my back picking up a ball.

289
00:17:42,314 --> 00:17:43,314
Oh my.

290
00:17:43,314 --> 00:17:46,644
I wasn't looking for Mom. Where's Heung Sik?

291
00:17:46,714 --> 00:17:48,554
Heung Sik? Oh my, there he is.

292
00:17:49,384 --> 00:17:50,384
Oh dear.

293
00:17:51,714 --> 00:17:53,414
- Heung Sik. - Gyeol.

294
00:17:54,014 --> 00:17:57,714
Oh dear, you said your back was acting up today too, right?

295
00:17:58,784 --> 00:17:59,814
This is perfect.

296
00:18:00,214 --> 00:18:02,344
There's a place for the two of you to go together.

297
00:18:03,184 --> 00:18:05,444
If you need to talk to Heung Sik, you can do it there.

298
00:18:05,554 --> 00:18:06,684
Okay?

299
00:18:07,784 --> 00:18:08,914
- Should we? - Yes.

300
00:18:09,014 --> 00:18:11,284
- Be careful. - Oh dear. My back is killing me.

301
00:18:18,644 --> 00:18:19,644
Heung Sik.

302
00:18:20,644 --> 00:18:22,084
What is it?

303
00:18:22,214 --> 00:18:24,214
Please answer my question honestly.

304
00:18:25,144 --> 00:18:26,944
This is a really, really important thing...

305
00:18:27,014 --> 00:18:28,214
in my eight years of life.

306
00:18:29,084 --> 00:18:30,414
Look me in the face.

307
00:18:33,784 --> 00:18:35,484
All right, ask away.

308
00:18:35,614 --> 00:18:39,184
The Game Man we met at the police station a few days ago,

309
00:18:40,014 --> 00:18:41,614
you've definitely met him before, right?

310
00:18:42,844 --> 00:18:45,814
No, I'd never seen him before.

311
00:18:47,514 --> 00:18:49,284
Then why were you so flustered?

312
00:18:50,344 --> 00:18:51,384
I wasn't.

313
00:18:51,714 --> 00:18:53,484
That's not what happened. You must have seen wrong.

314
00:18:53,614 --> 00:18:55,284
I told you to look me in the face.

315
00:18:59,084 --> 00:19:00,084
But...

316
00:19:00,554 --> 00:19:02,214
why is my mom acting so strange?

317
00:19:03,584 --> 00:19:04,614
What's strange about her?

318
00:19:05,144 --> 00:19:06,584
She doesn't seem strange at all to me.

319
00:19:06,744 --> 00:19:07,744
That's not true.

320
00:19:08,414 --> 00:19:10,084
After she met the Game Man, she's been a little...

321
00:19:11,214 --> 00:19:13,184
No, my mom's been very strange.

322
00:19:14,684 --> 00:19:15,684
That's not right.

323
00:19:16,014 --> 00:19:17,944
I saw her for a moment on the street this morning,

324
00:19:18,614 --> 00:19:20,084
and she seemed completely normal.

325
00:19:26,844 --> 00:19:28,684
My mom says she hates the Game Man.

326
00:19:29,914 --> 00:19:31,884
Would you expect her to like someone she met at a police station?

327
00:19:32,014 --> 00:19:33,514
She said, "I hate him because I hate him."

328
00:19:33,584 --> 00:19:34,614
What's that supposed to mean?

329
00:19:34,914 --> 00:19:36,414
What does "I hate him because I hate him" even mean?

330
00:19:36,484 --> 00:19:38,984
A negative plus a negative makes a strong positive, you know.

331
00:19:39,314 --> 00:19:41,344
It means she likes him a lot.

332
00:19:43,114 --> 00:19:44,244
No, that can't be right.

333
00:19:44,444 --> 00:19:47,084
Your mom said she'd completely gotten over that guy.

334
00:19:47,784 --> 00:19:50,514
Sure, they were crazy about each other back then,

335
00:19:50,584 --> 00:19:52,484
but that was eight years ago.

336
00:19:57,314 --> 00:19:58,314
Gyeol...

337
00:20:00,144 --> 00:20:01,914
I'm a little busy right now,

338
00:20:03,114 --> 00:20:05,384
so if we're done talking, do you mind if I go?

339
00:20:10,684 --> 00:20:12,414
Keep up the good work.

340
00:20:12,844 --> 00:20:13,844
Okay. Thanks.

341
00:21:04,644 --> 00:21:05,814
Hey, hey, hey.

342
00:21:07,014 --> 00:21:09,114
- Why are you throwing that out? - It tastes like garbage.

343
00:21:10,614 --> 00:21:11,644
Wait, hold on.

344
00:21:17,984 --> 00:21:20,114
What do you mean, garbage? This tastes great.

345
00:21:25,584 --> 00:21:28,054
In fact, it's the best thing you've made recently.

346
00:21:28,184 --> 00:21:30,944
- Don't overdo it. Give it back. - I'm not, seriously.

347
00:21:32,084 --> 00:21:34,144
I think there's something wrong with your taste buds right now.

348
00:21:38,844 --> 00:21:40,414
On second thought, this is a little off.

349
00:21:40,714 --> 00:21:42,584
- Give it. - Off the charts good.

350
00:21:42,644 --> 00:21:46,144
- Stop being so annoying. - It's honestly delicious.

351
00:21:46,484 --> 00:21:47,714
We can just let the others try it, right?

352
00:21:47,844 --> 00:21:49,114
Bring it here while I'm still being nice.

353
00:21:49,284 --> 00:21:51,084
This doesn't sound like you're being nice.

354
00:21:59,584 --> 00:22:01,984
You ordered side dishes and kimchi?

355
00:22:01,984 --> 00:22:02,984
Yes.

356
00:22:03,044 --> 00:22:04,114
- Yes. - Thanks.

357
00:22:04,514 --> 00:22:06,044
- Eight of each. - Hurry up and get ready to set up.

358
00:22:06,114 --> 00:22:07,114
Okay.

359
00:22:07,444 --> 00:22:08,484
Unpack them now.

360
00:22:12,914 --> 00:22:13,914
Hurry and try it.

361
00:22:17,514 --> 00:22:19,084
It's so good.

362
00:22:20,244 --> 00:22:21,714
- This is amazing. - Really?

363
00:22:22,814 --> 00:22:25,544
It's like my mom made this.

364
00:22:25,544 --> 00:22:27,084
Hey, I could eat two bowls of rice with just this.

365
00:22:27,084 --> 00:22:29,114
You eat two bowls of rice anyway.

366
00:22:29,744 --> 00:22:30,744
How did you know?

367
00:22:30,844 --> 00:22:32,584
- Isn't the Chef eating? - I don't know.

368
00:22:33,084 --> 00:22:35,044
Ma'am, this is so good.

369
00:22:36,844 --> 00:22:37,844
There.

370
00:22:40,944 --> 00:22:43,014
- Here you go. - You must be a great cook.

371
00:22:43,284 --> 00:22:44,914
Our guys are really picky eaters.

372
00:22:45,284 --> 00:22:46,384
Thank you.

373
00:22:46,884 --> 00:22:47,984
Please order often.

374
00:22:48,184 --> 00:22:51,084
We offer free delivery on orders over 50 dollars.

375
00:22:51,144 --> 00:22:53,284
If you become a regular, I'll throw in lots of freebies...

376
00:22:53,284 --> 00:22:54,584
and new menu items for you to try.

377
00:22:54,584 --> 00:22:55,584
Got it.

378
00:22:55,944 --> 00:22:58,084
- Enjoy your meal. - Thank you, ma'am.

379
00:22:58,084 --> 00:22:59,214
- It's really delicious. - This is amazing.

380
00:22:59,284 --> 00:23:02,044
- Thank you. - Excuse me, where's the restroom?

381
00:23:02,644 --> 00:23:04,084
Go that way and turn right.

382
00:23:04,444 --> 00:23:06,014
- Thank you. - You're welcome. Goodbye.

383
00:23:06,344 --> 00:23:07,344
I'm hungry.

384
00:23:07,484 --> 00:23:08,484
Go on, eat.

385
00:23:11,314 --> 00:23:13,984
- Why would you throw this away? - Why are you taking that out?

386
00:23:13,984 --> 00:23:15,384
Watch your tone.

387
00:23:15,884 --> 00:23:16,984
You're making me want to swear.

388
00:23:22,444 --> 00:23:24,444
Mom's Homemade Side Dishes suddenly closed down,

389
00:23:24,444 --> 00:23:27,344
so I ordered from a different place. And I think I hit the jackpot.

390
00:23:28,114 --> 00:23:30,244
This is a huge hit too. Here, try some of this.

391
00:23:30,314 --> 00:23:31,984
- What is it? - A new dish?

392
00:23:32,144 --> 00:23:33,214
That looks so good.

393
00:23:33,214 --> 00:23:35,144
It's terrible. Don't eat it...

394
00:23:36,414 --> 00:23:37,414
Go ahead.

395
00:23:41,084 --> 00:23:44,714
- Where's this from? - What is this? It's amazing.

396
00:23:44,714 --> 00:23:45,814
- It's so good. - It's so good.

397
00:23:45,814 --> 00:23:47,414
- Right? - You've got to be kidding me.

398
00:23:48,044 --> 00:23:49,584
See? I told you it was a hit.

399
00:23:55,414 --> 00:23:56,484
This place is a hit too.

400
00:23:56,544 --> 00:23:58,214
- Right? - It's the real deal.

401
00:23:58,284 --> 00:23:59,614
Mom's Homemade Side Dishes can't even compare.

402
00:24:00,244 --> 00:24:02,444
Mu Jin, you have to try this.

403
00:24:02,544 --> 00:24:04,684
It's even better than my mom's cooking. Can you believe it?

404
00:24:04,684 --> 00:24:06,114
I'm not eating that. Your hands are dirty.

405
00:24:06,744 --> 00:24:09,414
Fine, don't eat it. It's your loss.

406
00:24:10,814 --> 00:24:12,714
Seriously? This is incredible.

407
00:24:15,044 --> 00:24:16,684
- Sit down and eat. - Okay.

408
00:24:18,114 --> 00:24:19,144
What is it?

409
00:24:24,444 --> 00:24:25,714
This is Han Gyeol.

410
00:24:26,044 --> 00:24:29,014
If you're not busy, could we meet for a bit?

411
00:24:31,284 --> 00:24:34,344
Yes, we can. Absolutely.

412
00:24:39,584 --> 00:24:42,044
What's gotten into him all of a sudden? It's so unlike him.

413
00:24:45,114 --> 00:24:48,044
I'm just stepping out for a bit, so please enjoy your meal.

414
00:24:48,284 --> 00:24:50,384
Director, this dish.

415
00:24:50,384 --> 00:24:52,184
Let's consider adding it to the official menu.

416
00:24:52,244 --> 00:24:54,414
On second thought, I think it tasted pretty good.

417
00:24:55,414 --> 00:24:57,414
- Yes, Chef. - Eat up.

418
00:24:57,744 --> 00:24:59,544
- See you later. - See you.

419
00:25:03,814 --> 00:25:05,984
People who couldn't properly go through their teen rebellion...

420
00:25:06,044 --> 00:25:08,344
sometimes hit their midlife crisis a little early.

421
00:25:08,484 --> 00:25:10,014
Our chef has lost his mind.

422
00:25:10,084 --> 00:25:11,314
So don't just curse him under your breath.

423
00:25:11,414 --> 00:25:14,614
Let's just feel sorry for him. It's tragic, at his young age.

424
00:25:14,684 --> 00:25:15,844
- Okay. - All right, dig in, everyone.

425
00:25:16,114 --> 00:25:17,984
- Enjoy your meal. - You too.

426
00:25:21,344 --> 00:25:24,344
But seriously, where is this place? I'm tempted to steal the recipe...

427
00:25:24,344 --> 00:25:25,814
and pass it off as our own, right?

428
00:25:26,084 --> 00:25:27,084
Exactly.

429
00:26:00,214 --> 00:26:01,214
Here...

430
00:26:02,014 --> 00:26:03,444
This is Gyu Young's business card.

431
00:26:08,084 --> 00:26:12,214
Why don't you give Gyu Young a call? With her wedding coming up,

432
00:26:12,284 --> 00:26:14,914
she must be feeling so lost and anxious.

433
00:26:15,714 --> 00:26:18,584
And her sister is only one year older.

434
00:26:20,084 --> 00:26:22,284
I think there's a lot a mother should be helping with.

435
00:26:23,284 --> 00:26:26,014
(Cliad Clinic)

436
00:26:43,884 --> 00:26:45,784
I'm telling you, it's authentic.

437
00:26:46,084 --> 00:26:47,814
You saw the warranty, the certificate, and the receipt.

438
00:26:47,814 --> 00:26:49,314
You checked everything.

439
00:26:49,714 --> 00:26:52,844
You said you only used it three or four times,

440
00:26:53,044 --> 00:26:56,044
but now that I look closely, it seems to have a lot of scratches.

441
00:26:56,414 --> 00:26:58,544
I saw the same one online,

442
00:26:58,614 --> 00:27:02,444
and with this many scratches, it was about 1,000 dollars cheaper.

443
00:27:03,814 --> 00:27:05,244
In that case,

444
00:27:05,314 --> 00:27:07,414
why don't you go buy the one that's 1,000 dollars cheaper?

445
00:27:07,884 --> 00:27:08,884
No.

446
00:27:10,414 --> 00:27:14,644
It's just that I really love it. So maybe 700 or...

447
00:27:14,714 --> 00:27:17,584
could you take another 500 dollars off?

448
00:27:17,714 --> 00:27:19,044
I looked at your seller page,

449
00:27:19,114 --> 00:27:21,184
and you have a lot of other bags and shoes.

450
00:27:21,414 --> 00:27:23,284
I'll buy those from you later.

451
00:27:23,814 --> 00:27:25,384
And I'll even recommend you to my friends.

452
00:27:25,444 --> 00:27:27,344
Recommend me? Give me a break.

453
00:27:28,214 --> 00:27:30,844
What... What did you just say?

454
00:27:31,084 --> 00:27:32,084
What?

455
00:27:32,214 --> 00:27:34,314
So your friends can also drive me crazy,

456
00:27:34,384 --> 00:27:36,984
nitpick everything, and low ball me to get it for nothing?

457
00:27:37,284 --> 00:27:39,644
Forget it. I'm not selling it to you.

458
00:27:42,514 --> 00:27:44,014
Unbelievable.

459
00:27:44,844 --> 00:27:46,344
And you're just some person selling a bag.

460
00:27:51,244 --> 00:27:53,084
Okay, let's say I'm here selling a bag.

461
00:27:53,244 --> 00:27:55,244
Then what are you doing here? Selling off your conscience?

462
00:27:56,284 --> 00:27:58,114
Because of my situation, I had no choice...

463
00:27:58,184 --> 00:28:00,714
but to list this bag, in its great condition, for 1,000 dollars less.

464
00:28:01,344 --> 00:28:03,644
And you want me to cut another 1,000 dollars from that?

465
00:28:05,144 --> 00:28:08,144
I'd rather not sell it at all. This is disgusting.

466
00:28:09,644 --> 00:28:12,484
Look at you, already obsessed with designer brands at such a young age.

467
00:28:12,614 --> 00:28:13,644
Hey.

468
00:28:16,644 --> 00:28:18,014
What did you just say?

469
00:28:21,414 --> 00:28:24,444
All this designer stuff you're wearing from head to toe,

470
00:28:24,914 --> 00:28:26,714
you didn't buy it with your own money, did you?

471
00:28:27,384 --> 00:28:30,084
Did your parents buy it for you? Did your sugar daddy buy it?

472
00:28:30,844 --> 00:28:34,384
You're just a kid. You should be carrying an Eco-bag.

473
00:28:34,444 --> 00:28:36,684
That's more your speed, sweetie.

474
00:28:39,314 --> 00:28:40,984
You broke piece of trash.

475
00:28:41,714 --> 00:28:44,384
You're out here selling your bag because you're broke.

476
00:28:44,384 --> 00:28:47,314
Hey. You'd better figure out your place in this world.

477
00:28:47,384 --> 00:28:49,944
Unless you want to beg on the streets when you're old. Seriously.

478
00:28:50,584 --> 00:28:51,584
Hey.

479
00:28:52,514 --> 00:28:53,514
Darn it.

480
00:28:55,844 --> 00:28:57,084
My baby.

481
00:28:58,544 --> 00:28:59,784
Darn it.

482
00:29:15,744 --> 00:29:17,084
The one and only Han Gyu Young...

483
00:29:18,414 --> 00:29:21,244
How did I end up in this pathetic state?

484
00:29:36,084 --> 00:29:38,514
Whoever crosses me today is dead.

485
00:29:40,514 --> 00:29:41,514
Yes?

486
00:29:43,844 --> 00:29:44,844
Hello?

487
00:29:45,384 --> 00:29:46,384
Hello?

488
00:29:48,784 --> 00:29:50,444
Who is this? If you're going to call,

489
00:29:50,444 --> 00:29:52,114
you should say something.

490
00:29:53,244 --> 00:29:55,314
What is this? A prank call?

491
00:29:55,314 --> 00:29:56,544
You're dead.

492
00:29:56,644 --> 00:29:57,644
Where are you?

493
00:29:57,644 --> 00:29:58,714
What's your name?

494
00:29:59,314 --> 00:30:01,384
Is this Han Gyu Young's phone?

495
00:30:03,844 --> 00:30:05,884
It is. Who is this?

496
00:30:06,214 --> 00:30:07,344
Gyu Young.

497
00:30:08,844 --> 00:30:09,944
It's Mom.

498
00:30:21,984 --> 00:30:23,284
You're here.

499
00:30:47,584 --> 00:30:48,744
You are Gyu Young, right?

500
00:30:49,244 --> 00:30:50,284
Yes.

501
00:30:51,484 --> 00:30:52,944
It's been a while, Mom.

502
00:30:55,914 --> 00:30:58,144
- Let's sit. - Okay.

503
00:31:06,614 --> 00:31:08,514
You've gotten even more beautiful, Mom.

504
00:31:09,314 --> 00:31:10,544
And more elegant.

505
00:31:12,944 --> 00:31:15,314
I think I used to talk to you more casually.

506
00:31:15,644 --> 00:31:17,314
But it doesn't feel right to do that anymore.

507
00:31:17,814 --> 00:31:19,544
By the way, I became a doctor.

508
00:31:19,844 --> 00:31:22,144
I wanted to tell you proudly when I met you,

509
00:31:22,284 --> 00:31:24,414
so I studied really, really hard.

510
00:31:26,284 --> 00:31:27,684
I missed you, Mom.

511
00:31:31,914 --> 00:31:33,014
Why did you do that?

512
00:31:34,344 --> 00:31:35,344
Pardon?

513
00:31:37,884 --> 00:31:39,584
Here is your tea.

514
00:31:41,784 --> 00:31:43,144
What would you like, miss?

515
00:31:45,414 --> 00:31:47,744
I'll order in a little bit.

516
00:31:48,344 --> 00:31:49,344
Okay.

517
00:32:03,384 --> 00:32:05,114
Why did you go see my husband?

518
00:32:06,744 --> 00:32:10,044
If you had something to say, you should have come to me first.

519
00:32:11,144 --> 00:32:13,714
Why did you go to him? Not only that,

520
00:32:14,014 --> 00:32:15,814
you told him to keep it a secret from me.

521
00:32:18,984 --> 00:32:21,184
I'm sorry. I just...

522
00:32:22,044 --> 00:32:24,044
You remarried and are living well,

523
00:32:24,384 --> 00:32:26,814
so I was worried I'd make you uncomfortable if I just showed up.

524
00:32:26,884 --> 00:32:28,684
If you knew it would be uncomfortable,

525
00:32:29,344 --> 00:32:31,044
did you not think about what an awkward position...

526
00:32:31,044 --> 00:32:32,284
that would put me in?

527
00:32:34,484 --> 00:32:37,084
You're a doctor, and you don't even have that much common sense?

528
00:32:39,414 --> 00:32:40,484
I'm sorry.

529
00:32:41,144 --> 00:32:42,644
Does "sorry" make everything okay?

530
00:32:45,044 --> 00:32:47,344
I heard you even asked him to come to the family meeting.

531
00:32:48,914 --> 00:32:51,084
What is your father doing all this time?

532
00:32:52,384 --> 00:32:54,344
Is your father dead or something?

533
00:32:57,344 --> 00:32:58,914
If my father comes,

534
00:32:59,314 --> 00:33:01,184
I'm afraid he'll ruin my whole marriage.

535
00:33:01,884 --> 00:33:04,044
You know what he's like.

536
00:33:04,784 --> 00:33:06,084
My future husband's family...

537
00:33:06,414 --> 00:33:08,144
is a very prominent family.

538
00:33:09,384 --> 00:33:10,744
This is the first time I've ever hit the jackpot,

539
00:33:10,784 --> 00:33:12,344
and you have no idea how hard I worked to get here.

540
00:33:13,144 --> 00:33:15,314
This is a marriage that I have to make happen,

541
00:33:15,384 --> 00:33:17,744
so I asked the chairman, even though I knew it was rude.

542
00:33:17,884 --> 00:33:19,684
Do you hear yourself?

543
00:33:20,414 --> 00:33:21,644
How can you say that?

544
00:33:24,214 --> 00:33:27,184
How on earth did your father raise you all?

545
00:33:27,644 --> 00:33:30,514
Our father didn't raise us. We raised ourselves.

546
00:33:31,114 --> 00:33:32,444
And what about you, Mom?

547
00:33:32,914 --> 00:33:34,984
You're the one who ran away and left us when we were kids.

548
00:33:36,444 --> 00:33:38,084
I never ran away.

549
00:33:39,714 --> 00:33:42,614
I was kicked out by your father after he found another woman.

550
00:33:43,914 --> 00:33:45,984
I couldn't take Gyu Rim because she was the oldest daughter,

551
00:33:46,484 --> 00:33:48,214
and I couldn't take Gyu Oh because he was the son.

552
00:33:49,614 --> 00:33:51,244
I tried to leave with you, Gyu Young,

553
00:33:51,314 --> 00:33:52,584
but you're the one who said...

554
00:33:53,344 --> 00:33:55,944
you didn't want to go with your poor mother.

555
00:33:56,514 --> 00:33:58,284
You wanted to stay with your rich father.

556
00:34:08,914 --> 00:34:10,214
Here's ten thousand dollars.

557
00:34:12,114 --> 00:34:14,044
I'm sure you have a lot of expenses. Use this.

558
00:34:16,714 --> 00:34:17,784
Is that all?

559
00:34:19,684 --> 00:34:21,584
You're giving me ten thousand dollars and that's it?

560
00:34:22,044 --> 00:34:24,644
- Gyu Young. - We’re reunited after 17 years.

561
00:34:26,044 --> 00:34:27,884
What kind of mother are you?

562
00:34:30,884 --> 00:34:32,884
I thought you would at least cry when you saw me.

563
00:34:33,144 --> 00:34:35,114
I thought you would at least give me a hug.

564
00:34:36,314 --> 00:34:38,314
I thought you'd ask who I'm marrying,

565
00:34:38,544 --> 00:34:41,514
or if I was having a hard time.

566
00:34:48,954 --> 00:34:50,284
I heard...

567
00:34:51,714 --> 00:34:53,784
you asked my husband for help with the wedding ceremony.

568
00:34:55,714 --> 00:34:56,884
That's not happening.

569
00:34:57,284 --> 00:34:58,514
I won't let him go.

570
00:34:58,744 --> 00:35:02,044
- Mom. - We won't lose our minds like you.

571
00:35:04,014 --> 00:35:05,244
Then should I just call off the wedding?

572
00:35:05,644 --> 00:35:06,914
Even after our family meeting?

573
00:35:07,544 --> 00:35:09,614
You have to take responsibility for your own actions.

574
00:35:11,814 --> 00:35:13,144
You're an adult now.

575
00:35:16,954 --> 00:35:20,514
Mom, were you always this cold and cruel?

576
00:35:26,744 --> 00:35:27,744
Do you have...

577
00:35:29,314 --> 00:35:31,014
any idea how I got to where I am today?

578
00:35:34,784 --> 00:35:38,544
After being kicked out with nothing I hit rock bottom.

579
00:35:40,954 --> 00:35:42,714
How do you think I made it this far?

580
00:35:46,784 --> 00:35:50,414
My family now...

581
00:35:51,414 --> 00:35:52,914
is more precious to me than my own life.

582
00:35:54,914 --> 00:35:56,714
I don't want to lose them ever again.

583
00:36:00,084 --> 00:36:01,714
So please, help me out here.

584
00:36:03,844 --> 00:36:05,984
Don't ever contact my husband again.

585
00:36:13,814 --> 00:36:14,814
I'm begging you.

586
00:37:35,484 --> 00:37:37,314
- Hello. - Hey, Gigolo.

587
00:37:37,384 --> 00:37:39,684
Are you trying to get thrown in jail?

588
00:37:51,414 --> 00:37:52,954
The number you've called is now unavailable.

589
00:37:53,014 --> 00:37:54,744
This punk. You give him an inch, and he takes a mile.

590
00:37:57,244 --> 00:38:00,184
Fine. This isn't the only pay phone around.

591
00:38:01,084 --> 00:38:03,384
Let's see who wins this, you or me.

592
00:38:04,314 --> 00:38:06,954
I'll never give up before I take him down.

593
00:38:07,014 --> 00:38:08,014
Darn it.

594
00:38:12,784 --> 00:38:14,014
I think it's around here somewhere.

595
00:38:15,914 --> 00:38:19,684
Delicious side dishes for sale

596
00:38:19,744 --> 00:38:23,454
Come and get them

597
00:38:23,514 --> 00:38:24,514
Welcome...

598
00:38:25,684 --> 00:38:26,844
Grandma.

599
00:38:27,614 --> 00:38:28,844
Well now, who in the world is this?

600
00:38:29,414 --> 00:38:32,014
I'm sure I know you, don't I?

601
00:38:32,244 --> 00:38:33,914
It's me, Hee Na.

602
00:38:34,014 --> 00:38:36,344
Colonel Kwon Taek Soo's youngest daughter, Kwon Hee Na.

603
00:38:36,414 --> 00:38:38,514
Oh, that's right. Oh my goodness.

604
00:38:38,584 --> 00:38:40,414
Yes, Hee Na. It is you. It really is.

605
00:38:40,484 --> 00:38:44,644
- Oh my, how long has it been? - I'm sorry, Grandma.

606
00:38:44,714 --> 00:38:46,544
I wanted to come sooner. I'm so late, aren't I?

607
00:38:47,084 --> 00:38:48,984
My goodness, will you look at you.

608
00:38:49,484 --> 00:38:53,214
The last time I saw you, you were still just a little kid.

609
00:38:53,484 --> 00:38:56,044
You've now become a young lady.

610
00:38:56,114 --> 00:38:57,644
Let me see. Oh my.

611
00:38:59,184 --> 00:39:02,184
So, are your parents doing well?

612
00:39:02,614 --> 00:39:06,344
And your brother, Hee Seop is doing well too, right?

613
00:39:06,414 --> 00:39:07,454
Yes, of course.

614
00:39:07,514 --> 00:39:08,984
When I said I was coming to see you today,

615
00:39:09,044 --> 00:39:10,784
my whole family asked me to send their regards.

616
00:39:11,084 --> 00:39:12,084
Good, good.

617
00:39:12,814 --> 00:39:16,084
You must've graduated from school a while ago, right?

618
00:39:16,744 --> 00:39:17,744
Did you find a job?

619
00:39:18,244 --> 00:39:19,384
Oh, no.

620
00:39:19,454 --> 00:39:21,814
These days, if you go around asking things like that,

621
00:39:21,884 --> 00:39:23,454
people get offended.

622
00:39:27,244 --> 00:39:28,244
Ta-da.

623
00:39:28,544 --> 00:39:30,884
I became a teacher.

624
00:39:31,084 --> 00:39:33,954
At a nearby elementary school. I moved nearby too.

625
00:39:34,014 --> 00:39:38,484
Oh my goodness, Hee Na, you've done so well for yourself.

626
00:39:38,644 --> 00:39:41,784
Well, since you're here, take some side dishes with you.

627
00:39:41,844 --> 00:39:43,814
I'll pack the meat dishes you like.

628
00:39:43,884 --> 00:39:46,314
It's okay.

629
00:39:51,344 --> 00:39:52,344
Smell it.

630
00:39:54,084 --> 00:39:55,514
- It'll be delicious, right? - This is great.

631
00:39:57,244 --> 00:39:59,014
(Suragan Side Dishes)

632
00:39:59,184 --> 00:40:00,954
- Here. - I'll get going, Grandma.

633
00:40:00,954 --> 00:40:03,144
I'll be back for more before these run out.

634
00:40:03,214 --> 00:40:04,214
All right, dear.

635
00:40:04,414 --> 00:40:07,014
You have to eat well, especially when you live alone.

636
00:40:07,084 --> 00:40:08,914
Okay, I'm off. Goodbye.

637
00:40:08,984 --> 00:40:10,954
Hey, watch where you're going.

638
00:40:11,014 --> 00:40:12,184
Goodness, you'll fall.

639
00:40:14,114 --> 00:40:15,984
Oh, what a sweet girl.

640
00:40:16,544 --> 00:40:18,544
Oh my goodness. You scared me.

641
00:40:19,314 --> 00:40:22,714
You should make a sound when you show up. You scared me.

642
00:40:22,784 --> 00:40:25,454
My sister left her cell phone at home.

643
00:40:26,584 --> 00:40:29,544
Oh, dear, she left her phone at home?

644
00:40:30,084 --> 00:40:31,084
Wait.

645
00:40:31,214 --> 00:40:33,484
Why is this phone so cold?

646
00:40:34,954 --> 00:40:37,484
That's because it was in the freezer until a moment ago.

647
00:40:38,714 --> 00:40:41,014
Please just tell my sister it was stuck in a corner.

648
00:40:41,084 --> 00:40:42,084
And that it was hard to find.

649
00:40:47,714 --> 00:40:49,544
(Suragan Side Dishes)

650
00:40:49,784 --> 00:40:51,914
He's worried about embarrassing his sister.

651
00:40:52,284 --> 00:40:55,614
Such a thoughtful boy.

652
00:40:57,044 --> 00:41:01,084
Both of them are so lovely, from head to toe.

653
00:41:02,314 --> 00:41:04,814
So how did that brat get stuck in between them...

654
00:41:05,884 --> 00:41:07,584
Well, what do I care?

655
00:41:07,744 --> 00:41:09,114
It's not like she's going to be part of my family.

656
00:41:15,714 --> 00:41:17,184
Is he a stalker?

657
00:41:28,784 --> 00:41:29,784
You know who I am, right?

658
00:41:30,454 --> 00:41:31,714
No, I don't.

659
00:41:32,784 --> 00:41:33,784
You really don't know me?

660
00:41:34,114 --> 00:41:36,544
I told you, I don't. Who are you?

661
00:41:36,614 --> 00:41:37,984
Then why did you look so surprised a moment ago?

662
00:41:40,214 --> 00:41:41,244
What are you talking about?

663
00:41:41,984 --> 00:41:44,984
I don't know how tough you are,

664
00:41:45,184 --> 00:41:48,714
but when a normal person like me is followed by a stranger,

665
00:41:48,784 --> 00:41:49,884
and stared at like that,

666
00:41:49,954 --> 00:41:51,314
ten out of ten of them are going to be surprised.

667
00:41:53,544 --> 00:41:54,784
You really don't know who I am?

668
00:41:58,014 --> 00:41:59,954
Am I supposed to know who you are?

669
00:42:12,184 --> 00:42:16,644
I never should've gotten back together with that jerk.

670
00:42:20,954 --> 00:42:22,514
Why would you get back with an ex-boyfriend?

671
00:42:22,614 --> 00:42:24,014
I know, right?

672
00:42:24,084 --> 00:42:26,384
Why did I get back together with him?

673
00:42:29,514 --> 00:42:33,114
We broke up because he cheated on me.

674
00:42:34,184 --> 00:42:38,384
For a whole month, he begged and pleaded.

675
00:42:39,484 --> 00:42:41,614
He said he'd really change,

676
00:42:42,184 --> 00:42:46,144
and asked for just one more chance.

677
00:42:50,314 --> 00:42:51,644
So...

678
00:42:55,884 --> 00:42:59,284
I pretended to give in and took him back.

679
00:43:01,284 --> 00:43:05,084
Darn it, he did it again.

680
00:43:16,014 --> 00:43:17,844
If you just drink like that, you'll ruin your stomach.

681
00:43:18,014 --> 00:43:19,044
You should have some soup too.

682
00:43:28,744 --> 00:43:29,744
What?

683
00:43:32,084 --> 00:43:33,684
Are you...

684
00:43:34,584 --> 00:43:36,644
worried about me right now?

685
00:43:39,884 --> 00:43:40,884
Excuse me.

686
00:43:41,384 --> 00:43:42,384
Excuse me.

687
00:43:43,184 --> 00:43:44,184
You should wake up.

688
00:43:47,284 --> 00:43:48,284
Mom.

689
00:43:49,614 --> 00:43:50,614
Just...

690
00:43:51,944 --> 00:43:53,144
five more minutes.

691
00:43:53,844 --> 00:43:54,944
I'm going to sleep.

692
00:44:23,514 --> 00:44:24,514
Don't go.

693
00:44:28,084 --> 00:44:29,184
Don't leave me here,

694
00:44:30,714 --> 00:44:31,714
all alone.

695
00:44:33,414 --> 00:44:35,584
You're really drunk. Just go to sleep.

696
00:44:38,544 --> 00:44:40,244
Snap out of it. I'm not your boyfriend.

697
00:44:42,714 --> 00:44:43,714
I know.

698
00:44:44,484 --> 00:44:45,484
You're...

699
00:44:46,784 --> 00:44:47,784
Han Gyu Oh.

700
00:46:39,344 --> 00:46:40,344
It's been a while,

701
00:46:41,044 --> 00:46:42,044
Han Gyu Oh.

702
00:46:51,584 --> 00:46:54,314
Oh, I haven't seen you in a while.

703
00:46:54,744 --> 00:46:57,184
- It's been a couple months, right? - Yes.

704
00:46:57,684 --> 00:47:00,614
But have you been sick? You look a little thinner.

705
00:47:01,244 --> 00:47:02,414
No, I haven't been sick,

706
00:47:02,544 --> 00:47:04,084
but I just haven't had an appetite lately.

707
00:47:04,714 --> 00:47:06,344
But for some reason, I can eat the noodles here.

708
00:47:06,644 --> 00:47:08,384
If I'd known, I would've come a few days sooner.

709
00:47:08,384 --> 00:47:09,814
Oh, that's a relief.

710
00:47:10,084 --> 00:47:11,414
- Enjoy your meal. - Okay.

711
00:47:11,414 --> 00:47:13,784
- Let me know if you need anything. - Okay.

712
00:47:19,614 --> 00:47:20,614
Please have a seat here.

713
00:47:30,184 --> 00:47:32,684
- Excuse me, I'll share this table. - Sure.

714
00:47:35,514 --> 00:47:37,414
- Knife-cut noodle soup, please. - Okay.

715
00:47:48,944 --> 00:47:51,714
I happened to try the noodles here a while ago,

716
00:47:52,414 --> 00:47:54,144
and I couldn't stop thinking about them, so I came back.

717
00:47:54,544 --> 00:47:55,544
I see.

718
00:48:01,814 --> 00:48:02,814
This spicy radish salad.

719
00:48:05,044 --> 00:48:07,384
You should try eating it with the spicy radish salad.

720
00:48:07,444 --> 00:48:08,744
It's absolutely incredible.

721
00:48:09,114 --> 00:48:10,114
Okay.

722
00:48:14,344 --> 00:48:18,044
Here, trust me and give it a try.

723
00:48:18,914 --> 00:48:19,914
Okay.

724
00:48:24,714 --> 00:48:25,714
Do I perhaps...

725
00:48:26,384 --> 00:48:28,414
look like an untrustworthy person?

726
00:48:30,244 --> 00:48:31,684
I just wanted you to enjoy your meal even more,

727
00:48:31,744 --> 00:48:35,544
so I worked up the courage, to give you a little advice.

728
00:48:36,544 --> 00:48:39,814
At least consider my sincerity, and give it a try.

729
00:48:40,544 --> 00:48:43,214
It's a flavour that's to die for, really.

730
00:49:00,284 --> 00:49:01,344
It's delicious, right?

731
00:49:02,044 --> 00:49:03,144
Much better, isn't it?

732
00:49:05,384 --> 00:49:06,384
Yes.

733
00:49:06,944 --> 00:49:08,384
See? What did I tell you?

734
00:49:09,114 --> 00:49:10,884
Here's your noodle soup.

735
00:49:12,814 --> 00:49:15,084
- A bowl of rice too, please. - Yes.

736
00:49:15,244 --> 00:49:17,184
- Enjoy your meal. - Thank you.

737
00:49:37,844 --> 00:49:40,084
This is the stuff.

738
00:49:40,314 --> 00:49:42,014
- Here's your rice. - Thanks.

739
00:49:50,614 --> 00:49:51,614
Now,

740
00:49:53,184 --> 00:49:55,314
let's move on to something even more delicious.

741
00:49:57,314 --> 00:49:58,314
If you eat this,

742
00:49:58,744 --> 00:50:00,784
and die from how good it is, I'm not responsible.

743
00:50:01,784 --> 00:50:02,784
Oh my.

744
00:50:03,384 --> 00:50:04,384
Now, like this...

745
00:50:08,244 --> 00:50:09,444
What do you think you're doing?

746
00:50:11,014 --> 00:50:12,614
Well, the spicy radish salad is good,

747
00:50:13,284 --> 00:50:15,184
but the true value of this noodle soup...

748
00:50:15,384 --> 00:50:18,414
is when you mix in some white rice like so.

749
00:50:18,484 --> 00:50:19,484
Hey.

750
00:50:20,184 --> 00:50:21,244
How can you just dump rice...

751
00:50:21,314 --> 00:50:23,444
into someone else's soup without even asking?

752
00:50:25,084 --> 00:50:26,084
Well, I just...

753
00:50:26,584 --> 00:50:28,144
I thought it was so delicious.

754
00:50:29,084 --> 00:50:30,384
Since we're sharing a table,

755
00:50:30,614 --> 00:50:32,144
I thought we could share a bite of rice...

756
00:50:32,214 --> 00:50:34,514
Then you can mix it into your own soup and eat it.

757
00:50:36,444 --> 00:50:38,984
What is this? It looks like dog food.

758
00:50:39,814 --> 00:50:40,814
Unbelievable.

759
00:50:41,184 --> 00:50:42,814
He's such a weirdo, seriously.

760
00:50:44,084 --> 00:50:46,044
- Seriously. - Ma'am.

761
00:50:46,484 --> 00:50:47,484
Excuse me, ma'am.

762
00:50:51,244 --> 00:50:52,384
Unbelievable.

763
00:50:54,244 --> 00:50:55,244
I mean...

764
00:50:55,444 --> 00:50:58,414
Is that really something to get so angry about?

765
00:50:59,184 --> 00:51:01,984
In this tough world, I was just saying we should share good things.

766
00:51:02,684 --> 00:51:03,684
Is that so wrong?

767
00:51:05,484 --> 00:51:06,844
Oh, come on.

768
00:51:08,044 --> 00:51:09,544
If dog food tastes this good,

769
00:51:09,944 --> 00:51:11,914
I'd eat it for the rest of my life.

770
00:51:12,984 --> 00:51:14,014
Seriously.

771
00:51:17,844 --> 00:51:18,884
It's delicious, though.

772
00:51:21,644 --> 00:51:23,214
Did you just have knife-cut noodle soup?

773
00:51:24,884 --> 00:51:26,084
You should have gone with me.

774
00:51:26,314 --> 00:51:28,214
I was just thinking about that place's noodle soup.

775
00:51:28,484 --> 00:51:29,684
Isn't it so rude?

776
00:51:30,514 --> 00:51:31,514
Me?

777
00:51:32,414 --> 00:51:34,814
No, he was a complete stranger.

778
00:51:34,914 --> 00:51:36,384
He put rice in my soup without asking.

779
00:51:36,444 --> 00:51:37,614
Is he out of his mind?

780
00:51:38,184 --> 00:51:40,514
It wasn't his soup. It was mine.

781
00:51:41,884 --> 00:51:44,584
Wait, who would put rice in your soup...

782
00:51:44,644 --> 00:51:45,944
without asking, Mom?

783
00:51:46,214 --> 00:51:50,284
I should have just shoved his face right in the soup.

784
00:51:50,344 --> 00:51:52,914
Then again, adding rice to their noodle soup...

785
00:51:52,984 --> 00:51:54,944
is the best way to eat it, honestly.

786
00:51:55,014 --> 00:51:57,914
Hey, you think I don't know that?

787
00:51:58,284 --> 00:52:00,084
Dr. Jeong told me to watch my carbs,

788
00:52:00,144 --> 00:52:01,684
and he won't stop nagging me about it,

789
00:52:01,744 --> 00:52:03,444
so I'm trying my best to cut back.

790
00:52:05,084 --> 00:52:07,984
That place is so popular that all sorts of people go there.

791
00:52:08,844 --> 00:52:11,644
Just chalk it up to a weird experience and forget it.

792
00:52:12,484 --> 00:52:14,384
Getting stressed only hurts you.

793
00:52:15,514 --> 00:52:16,644
Seriously.

794
00:52:17,084 --> 00:52:19,544
It was my first decent meal in a while,

795
00:52:19,684 --> 00:52:21,114
and that jerk ruined it.

796
00:52:22,184 --> 00:52:25,684
And he looked like a drowned rat.

797
00:52:26,714 --> 00:52:28,114
You mean he was that cute?

798
00:52:28,184 --> 00:52:29,584
(Chairman Hong Ok Seon)

799
00:52:29,644 --> 00:52:31,644
Hey, aren't you busy? Go on. Get to work.

800
00:52:50,984 --> 00:52:51,984
Who is it?

801
00:52:55,244 --> 00:52:56,244
Who's there?

802
00:52:58,984 --> 00:52:59,984
Seo Hyun.

803
00:53:01,984 --> 00:53:04,714
If you're home, come in. Why are you just standing there?

804
00:53:04,944 --> 00:53:06,584
Oh, Mom. It's you.

805
00:53:09,444 --> 00:53:10,584
Have you been drinking?

806
00:53:11,884 --> 00:53:14,414
Not a lot, just a little.

807
00:53:18,784 --> 00:53:20,114
This doesn't look like a little.

808
00:53:23,744 --> 00:53:24,744
What's wrong?

809
00:53:25,884 --> 00:53:27,444
Did something happen at work?

810
00:53:29,014 --> 00:53:30,714
Nothing happened at work.

811
00:53:33,484 --> 00:53:36,214
Mom, should I just move to another country?

812
00:53:37,344 --> 00:53:39,244
- What? - Never mind.

813
00:53:39,714 --> 00:53:40,714
Why should I leave to make them happy?

814
00:53:40,884 --> 00:53:42,114
Why should I?

815
00:53:43,614 --> 00:53:44,644
Kim Mu Jin.

816
00:53:44,984 --> 00:53:49,544
That rotten jerk. That complete idiot.

817
00:53:50,184 --> 00:53:51,184
What?

818
00:53:51,644 --> 00:53:52,744
What's the matter?

819
00:53:53,784 --> 00:53:55,614
Why are you crying?

820
00:53:56,644 --> 00:53:58,044
What did Mu Jin say to you?

821
00:53:59,484 --> 00:54:00,484
Mom.

822
00:54:00,914 --> 00:54:02,084
Am I really that terrible?

823
00:54:02,644 --> 00:54:03,684
No.

824
00:54:03,914 --> 00:54:05,644
Why would you be terrible?

825
00:54:06,244 --> 00:54:08,684
Oh, honey. You're the most precious...

826
00:54:08,744 --> 00:54:11,084
and beautiful girl in the world. How could you be terrible?

827
00:54:11,784 --> 00:54:13,614
Did Mu Jin say something that awful to you?

828
00:54:14,714 --> 00:54:17,714
He didn't, but it feels that way.

829
00:54:18,344 --> 00:54:19,814
Otherwise, how could he do this to me?

830
00:54:20,084 --> 00:54:21,084
He knows that I love him,

831
00:54:21,144 --> 00:54:22,944
and that I've only had eyes for him and waited.

832
00:54:23,014 --> 00:54:24,714
The moment that woman showed up,

833
00:54:24,784 --> 00:54:28,014
how could he be so easily swayed again?

834
00:54:28,244 --> 00:54:29,314
That woman?

835
00:54:30,814 --> 00:54:31,814
Don't tell me...

836
00:54:32,344 --> 00:54:35,544
the girl Mu Jin used to see showed up again.

837
00:54:40,284 --> 00:54:43,914
See? This is why I told you not to date Mu Jin.

838
00:54:44,444 --> 00:54:48,644
You're far too good for him. After how I raised you?

839
00:54:53,784 --> 00:54:56,444
He can't even appreciate how wonderful and beautiful you are.

840
00:54:56,514 --> 00:54:57,884
He only causes you pain.

841
00:54:58,314 --> 00:55:00,284
Even if he likes you now, I'm against it.

842
00:55:00,414 --> 00:55:04,114
Men a thousand times more handsome, amazing,

843
00:55:04,214 --> 00:55:06,014
smart, and kind than him,

844
00:55:06,084 --> 00:55:07,944
and men who would be absolutely crazy about you,

845
00:55:08,014 --> 00:55:09,844
I will line them all up for you,

846
00:55:10,114 --> 00:55:12,214
so you can just go ahead and dump a guy like Kim Mu Jin.

847
00:55:12,784 --> 00:55:14,084
If it were that easy, I wouldn't have been...

848
00:55:14,144 --> 00:55:15,514
stuck like this for the past 23 years.

849
00:55:18,584 --> 00:55:19,644
Jang Seo Hyun.

850
00:55:20,514 --> 00:55:23,684
Why are you acting like this? You're upsetting me.

851
00:55:26,544 --> 00:55:27,784
Don't tell Dad.

852
00:55:28,384 --> 00:55:29,384
I'm going to take a shower.

853
00:55:31,384 --> 00:55:32,384
Seo Hyun.

854
00:55:37,284 --> 00:55:38,484
That rotten punk.

855
00:55:45,214 --> 00:55:47,684
(Jung Woo)

856
00:55:51,784 --> 00:55:54,244
Jung Woo. This is Seo Hyun's mother.

857
00:55:55,144 --> 00:55:58,384
That girl Mu Jin used to see, I hear she's shown up again?

858
00:55:59,084 --> 00:56:01,244
What is she like, anyway? What does she do?

859
00:56:02,184 --> 00:56:04,014
And what do her parents do?

860
00:56:06,284 --> 00:56:08,784
You know what, instead of just pressing Mu Jin,

861
00:56:08,844 --> 00:56:10,444
I think I need to meet her myself.

862
00:56:11,444 --> 00:56:13,044
I'm just curious.

863
00:56:13,084 --> 00:56:15,984
Just what's so great about her compared to my Seo Hyun?

864
00:56:16,284 --> 00:56:18,384
I need to see it with my own two eyes.

865
00:56:19,844 --> 00:56:22,714
You have her name and phone number, right?

866
00:56:31,114 --> 00:56:32,814
(Dad)

867
00:56:37,914 --> 00:56:40,214
Dad, if it's not urgent, I'll call you back later.

868
00:56:40,484 --> 00:56:42,284
Hey. It is urgent.

869
00:56:42,914 --> 00:56:45,084
Gyu Young is giving the youngest ones a hard time.

870
00:56:45,484 --> 00:56:47,514
So I need you to come over and stop her, Gyu Rim.

871
00:56:49,144 --> 00:56:51,744
Then you should be the one to scold Gyu Young and tell her to stop, Dad.

872
00:56:51,914 --> 00:56:53,844
Does she listen to me?

873
00:56:54,184 --> 00:56:55,784
She acts like my words are just a dog barking.

874
00:56:56,344 --> 00:57:00,514
I'm scared she'll turn on me, so I'm calling from the rooftop.

875
00:57:00,784 --> 00:57:01,844
Is Gyu Oh not there either?

876
00:57:02,114 --> 00:57:03,984
No, so hurry up and get here.

877
00:57:04,484 --> 00:57:06,814
I'm telling you, it's an emergency. It's a Code Red.

878
00:57:12,444 --> 00:57:14,184
What are you going to do about this?

879
00:57:15,384 --> 00:57:16,514
I'll take responsibility for it.

880
00:57:17,184 --> 00:57:18,684
How are you going to take responsibility?

881
00:57:18,814 --> 00:57:20,044
Do you even know how much this costs?

882
00:57:20,244 --> 00:57:22,884
This is a limited-edition piece that's not even sold anymore.

883
00:57:23,884 --> 00:57:25,244
Did Gyu Seo do it on purpose?

884
00:57:25,814 --> 00:57:27,484
No, if it's such a precious item,

885
00:57:27,544 --> 00:57:29,384
you should have kept it separate from the family's laundry,

886
00:57:29,714 --> 00:57:31,214
and had it dry-cleaned.

887
00:57:32,314 --> 00:57:33,514
You didn't take proper care of it yourself,

888
00:57:33,584 --> 00:57:35,184
but you're always making a fuss about the laundry.

889
00:57:37,884 --> 00:57:38,884
Yourself?

890
00:57:39,184 --> 00:57:41,544
Hey. Did you just call me that?

891
00:57:41,644 --> 00:57:43,014
Yes, I did.

892
00:57:43,884 --> 00:57:47,314
You always call Gyu Rim "hey" and "you," so what's the big deal?

893
00:57:47,644 --> 00:57:48,644
Why can't I do it?

894
00:57:48,744 --> 00:57:49,744
Gyu Min.

895
00:57:50,014 --> 00:57:53,714
Besides, you don't even consider Gyu Seo and me your siblings anyway.

896
00:57:54,014 --> 00:57:55,084
You little...

897
00:57:55,244 --> 00:57:57,144
Stop, Gyu Young.

898
00:57:58,744 --> 00:58:00,844
Fine. If you want to pull my hair, go ahead.

899
00:58:00,914 --> 00:58:02,284
If you need to get your anger out, take it out on me.

900
00:58:02,344 --> 00:58:03,614
Just leave Gyu Seo out of this.

901
00:58:03,684 --> 00:58:07,784
- Go on, pull it all out. - Do you want to get killed? Hey.

902
00:58:07,844 --> 00:58:09,484
- Unbelievable. - What are you all doing?

903
00:58:10,384 --> 00:58:12,084
Hey, let go of her right now.

904
00:58:15,844 --> 00:58:17,014
What do you think you're doing?

905
00:58:17,444 --> 00:58:18,744
Why are you hitting Gyu Min?

906
00:58:18,984 --> 00:58:20,544
What gives you the right to lay a hand on her?

907
00:58:20,614 --> 00:58:22,484
If you don't know what's going on, then shut up and stay out of it.

908
00:58:22,644 --> 00:58:23,784
It was my fault.

909
00:58:24,084 --> 00:58:26,314
I was trying to finish the laundry before you got home,

910
00:58:26,884 --> 00:58:28,384
but I guess Gyu Young's clothes got mixed in.

911
00:58:29,184 --> 00:58:31,714
It's one of her favourite outfits, and it got badly stained.

912
00:58:31,784 --> 00:58:33,544
And that gives you the right to pull her hair?

913
00:58:34,044 --> 00:58:37,084
How many times have I told you to do your laundry separately?

914
00:58:37,714 --> 00:58:39,114
This is your fault,

915
00:58:39,184 --> 00:58:40,714
so who are you taking your anger out on?

916
00:58:45,944 --> 00:58:47,014
This.

917
00:58:49,014 --> 00:58:50,284
It's just like those twins.

918
00:58:50,344 --> 00:58:51,644
Do you know how disgusting that makes me feel?

919
00:58:52,444 --> 00:58:54,344
The things I like, the things I cherish.

920
00:58:55,444 --> 00:58:57,444
When they get involved, everything gets messed up like this.

921
00:58:58,314 --> 00:59:01,144
Your very existence feels like a stain on my life,

922
00:59:01,214 --> 00:59:02,514
and it's a horrible feeling.

923
00:59:02,584 --> 00:59:03,584
Han Gyu Young.

924
00:59:04,314 --> 00:59:05,444
Watch your mouth.

925
00:59:05,514 --> 00:59:07,044
If it weren't for them in the first place,

926
00:59:09,084 --> 00:59:10,144
if it weren't for their mother,

927
00:59:10,214 --> 00:59:11,384
our mom wouldn't have gotten a divorce...

928
00:59:11,444 --> 00:59:13,014
and have left us,

929
00:59:13,214 --> 00:59:15,484
and our family wouldn't have been completely ruined.

930
00:59:15,584 --> 00:59:17,244
I told you to watch your mouth.

931
00:59:17,984 --> 00:59:20,584
You two, go inside. She's completely lost it.

932
00:59:20,644 --> 00:59:23,014
There's no reason to listen to someone who's crazy. Get inside.

933
00:59:23,084 --> 00:59:24,414
- Hey. - Let's go.

934
00:59:24,414 --> 00:59:26,214
Let go. I want to hear what else she has to say.

935
00:59:26,544 --> 00:59:27,544
Gyu Min.

936
00:59:27,744 --> 00:59:28,884
Go inside, Gyu Min.

937
00:59:29,284 --> 00:59:30,644
I'll take care of everything.

938
00:59:32,084 --> 00:59:33,644
Whose side are you on?

939
00:59:33,744 --> 00:59:35,914
You're supposed to be on my side.

940
00:59:36,644 --> 00:59:38,014
We're full-blooded sisters,

941
00:59:38,084 --> 00:59:39,884
and they're the children of our sworn enemy.

942
00:59:39,944 --> 00:59:41,484
Shut up, Han Gyu Young.

943
00:59:42,884 --> 00:59:43,884
Han Gyu Rim.

944
00:59:45,244 --> 00:59:47,084
You're impossible.

945
00:59:47,484 --> 00:59:49,244
I thought you could be fixed,

946
00:59:49,384 --> 00:59:51,644
but I see now you're just trash that can't even be recycled.

947
00:59:52,314 --> 00:59:53,314
Han Gyu Rim.

948
00:59:53,444 --> 00:59:54,514
Get out of this house right now.

949
00:59:54,584 --> 00:59:56,544
- Hey. - Dad.

950
00:59:56,614 --> 01:00:01,284
I've never had a sister like her, so disown this girl immediately.

951
01:00:03,084 --> 01:00:05,084
I'll be disowned as soon as I get married anyway,

952
01:00:05,184 --> 01:00:07,344
- so don't worry. - Right now.

953
01:00:07,684 --> 01:00:09,014
Get out right now.

954
01:00:10,884 --> 01:00:12,514
I can't stand the sight of you for another second,

955
01:00:12,784 --> 01:00:13,814
so get out now.

956
01:00:14,244 --> 01:00:15,984
You think I won't get out if you tell me to?

957
01:00:16,284 --> 01:00:18,884
I don't want to be in this miserable house for another second either.

958
01:00:25,484 --> 01:00:26,544
Gyu Rim.

959
01:00:29,344 --> 01:00:30,414
Oh, for goodness' sake.

960
01:00:34,084 --> 01:00:35,984
Do you want some water?

961
01:00:37,084 --> 01:00:38,184
Or how about a drink?

962
01:00:38,344 --> 01:00:39,384
Want a drink?

963
01:00:40,444 --> 01:00:43,084
No, I just got back from work and have to go out again.

964
01:00:43,584 --> 01:00:44,584
Right.

965
01:00:50,714 --> 01:00:52,114
When I get home from work,

966
01:00:52,414 --> 01:00:54,914
I'd love some of that spicy tteokbokki you make.

967
01:00:55,384 --> 01:00:56,414
Can you make some for me?

968
01:00:58,614 --> 01:01:00,614
Of course.

969
01:01:02,084 --> 01:01:03,644
Thanks for doing the laundry, Gyu Seo.

970
01:01:04,244 --> 01:01:06,984
Only you would do the laundry for me.

971
01:01:08,044 --> 01:01:09,184
It was no big deal.

972
01:01:16,844 --> 01:01:18,044
I'm the one who deserves to die.

973
01:01:19,944 --> 01:01:23,344
- Next one. - Summer or winter. One, two, three.

974
01:01:23,484 --> 01:01:24,484
- Winter. - Winter.

975
01:01:26,784 --> 01:01:27,784
You like winter?

976
01:01:27,844 --> 01:01:28,844
Yes.

977
01:01:29,544 --> 01:01:31,314
We've had seven questions so far,

978
01:01:31,384 --> 01:01:34,084
- and all seven were the same. - I know.

979
01:01:36,684 --> 01:01:39,314
Have you ever taken an MBTI test?

980
01:01:39,714 --> 01:01:41,284
Yes. Let's say our types at the same time.

981
01:01:41,414 --> 01:01:43,384
Okay. One, two, three.

982
01:01:43,444 --> 01:01:44,444
- ISFJ. - ISFJ.

983
01:01:45,614 --> 01:01:46,644
ISFJ?

984
01:01:47,084 --> 01:01:49,884
So that's what people call it.

985
01:01:51,314 --> 01:01:53,884
But sometimes my third letter comes out as T.

986
01:01:54,384 --> 01:01:55,814
You too?

987
01:01:55,884 --> 01:01:58,184
Me too, like when I'm studying or something.

988
01:01:59,284 --> 01:02:01,244
For me, it's when I'm at work...

989
01:02:02,444 --> 01:02:03,984
or when I have to deal with people I don't like.

990
01:02:04,184 --> 01:02:05,714
No way, me too.

991
01:02:07,584 --> 01:02:09,014
We're totally on the same wavelength.

992
01:02:09,744 --> 01:02:10,744
Totally.

993
01:02:11,984 --> 01:02:13,814
What is this? Are we on the same wavelength?

994
01:02:26,784 --> 01:02:29,514
I'm telling you, I could tell right away.

995
01:02:30,084 --> 01:02:32,814
That's right. Even within Jeolla Province,

996
01:02:32,884 --> 01:02:35,114
the southern region has its own distinct flavour.

997
01:02:36,584 --> 01:02:39,414
That's true. As expected, you get it.

998
01:02:39,984 --> 01:02:42,384
My goodness, where are you from, ma'am?

999
01:02:42,444 --> 01:02:43,514
I'm from near Wando.

1000
01:02:43,584 --> 01:02:46,714
My goodness, Wando? I'm from near Jindo.

1001
01:02:47,084 --> 01:02:49,714
Wando is where my husband is from.

1002
01:02:50,084 --> 01:02:53,214
But right after Heung Sik was born, we moved straight to Busan.

1003
01:02:53,384 --> 01:02:55,984
It all makes sense now.

1004
01:02:56,214 --> 01:02:58,884
The moment I tasted your side dishes at lunch,

1005
01:02:59,084 --> 01:03:01,284
I said, "Oh my, Mom." I'm telling you.

1006
01:03:02,384 --> 01:03:04,014
Can you believe that right after work,

1007
01:03:04,084 --> 01:03:05,484
I grabbed the receipt and a plastic bag,

1008
01:03:05,544 --> 01:03:07,444
and came all the way here to find you?

1009
01:03:07,784 --> 01:03:10,644
Well, out of everything, what was the most delicious?

1010
01:03:10,884 --> 01:03:15,244
Come on now. How could I possibly pick just one?

1011
01:03:16,014 --> 01:03:20,584
But if I had to choose just one,

1012
01:03:20,644 --> 01:03:22,514
the seasoned skate?

1013
01:03:23,684 --> 01:03:27,784
What should I do? We're all sold out of that.

1014
01:03:28,584 --> 01:03:31,614
Gosh, I'd just whip some up for you if I could,

1015
01:03:31,684 --> 01:03:33,814
but I'm not the one who made it.

1016
01:03:34,084 --> 01:03:36,514
For that seasoned skate, our Gyeol's Mom has to make it...

1017
01:03:36,584 --> 01:03:38,784
for it to taste just right.

1018
01:03:39,384 --> 01:03:43,584
Gyeol's Mom? So she's your daughter-in-law?

1019
01:03:44,084 --> 01:03:45,944
It's amazing how a mother and daughter-in-law...

1020
01:03:46,014 --> 01:03:49,014
- can both be such amazing cooks. - Not yet.

1021
01:03:49,084 --> 01:03:51,014
She's not my daughter-in-law.

1022
01:03:51,544 --> 01:03:54,344
Well, maybe in the future she could be.

1023
01:03:54,414 --> 01:03:56,944
If that happened, I'd be thrilled.

1024
01:03:57,244 --> 01:04:01,714
But that's just my own wishful thinking, you know?

1025
01:04:03,284 --> 01:04:04,684
Look.

1026
01:04:04,944 --> 01:04:06,384
My wishful thinking.

1027
01:04:07,444 --> 01:04:08,444
You're here?

1028
01:04:12,314 --> 01:04:13,344
Gyu Rim.

1029
01:04:17,944 --> 01:04:20,044
- Mister. - Yes?

1030
01:04:22,044 --> 01:04:23,484
You know my mom well, right?

1031
01:04:25,914 --> 01:04:28,684
A long time ago, I mean, eight years ago,

1032
01:04:29,414 --> 01:04:31,184
you met my mom, didn't you?

1033
01:04:41,844 --> 01:04:43,314
I knew it.

1034
01:04:45,244 --> 01:04:47,044
Did you like my mom?

1035
01:05:23,984 --> 01:05:25,684
(Love on the Menu)

1036
01:05:26,014 --> 01:05:28,814
Because I'd like to have a dad now too.

1037
01:05:28,884 --> 01:05:31,014
By suddenly jumping into Han Gyu Rim's life like this,

1038
01:05:31,014 --> 01:05:33,514
I don't have the right to shake things up.

1039
01:05:33,984 --> 01:05:35,614
Just buy it from another store.

1040
01:05:36,044 --> 01:05:37,084
Just sell it to me.

1041
01:05:37,084 --> 01:05:39,984
- Gyu Young, what are you doing? - Please save me, Chairman.

1042
